    "source": "1800 census at the census date, free adult men outside the Southern states; the census gives free white males in bands (16\u201326, 26\u201345, 45+), so men 21+ are split from the 16\u201326 band. Voters were men meeting each state's rules: most states required a freehold, property or taxpaying qualification (Vermont and Kentucky did not). Electors were chosen by popular vote in 6 states; elsewhere (Connecticut, Delaware, Georgia, Massachusetts, New Hampshire, New Jersey, New York, South Carolina and Vermont, with Pennsylvania's divided legislature splitting its electors by compromise) men cast no presidential vote. Free Black men could vote in some Northern states on the same or stricter terms."
   },
